From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:20:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] flow: SETUP_REPAIR_EFFORT passes -effort to repair_timing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

repair_timing's PARALLEL_EVAL policy takes -effort low, medium or high:
how soon a stalled batch stops and how much work goes into the worst
endpoints' tail. ORFS could already select the policy
(SETUP_REPAIR_PHASES=PARALLEL_EVAL) but not its effort, so a flow ran
it at the default, high, in every stage.

SETUP_REPAIR_EFFORT passes -effort to every repair_timing_helper call,
in floorplan, place, cts and global route; per stage through the build
system's stage arguments. Unset, nothing is passed and repair_timing
behaves as before. Set with another policy, repair_timing warns that it
has no effect (RSZ-3244).

Not upstreamed. Carried in bazel-orfs; retires on the //:bump onto an
ORFS that has it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 flow/scripts/util.tcl       |  1 +
 flow/scripts/variables.yaml | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/flow/scripts/util.tcl b/flow/scripts/util.tcl
index 4c023bed5..1c2239be5 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/util.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/util.tcl
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@ proc repair_timing_helper { args } {
   append_env_var additional_args HOLD_SLACK_MARGIN -hold_margin 1
   append_env_var additional_args SETUP_MOVE_SEQUENCE -sequence 1
   append_env_var additional_args SETUP_REPAIR_PHASES -phases 1
+  append_env_var additional_args SETUP_REPAIR_EFFORT -effort 1
   append_env_var additional_args TNS_END_PERCENT -repair_tns 1
   append_env_var additional_args SKIP_PIN_SWAP -skip_pin_swap 0
   append_env_var additional_args SKIP_GATE_CLONING -skip_gate_cloning 0
diff --git a/flow/scripts/variables.yaml b/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
index 11a7c7019..22c0b8e45 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
+++ b/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
@@ -916,6 +916,17 @@ SETUP_MOVE_SEQUENCE:
     - cts
     - floorplan
     - grt
+SETUP_REPAIR_EFFORT:
+  description: >
+    Passed as -effort to repair_timing: low, medium or high. It tunes the
+    PARALLEL_EVAL policy only (set SETUP_REPAIR_PHASES to PARALLEL_EVAL);
+    with another policy repair_timing warns and ignores it. When unset,
+    repair_timing uses its default effort.
+  stages:
+    - cts
+    - floorplan
+    - grt
+    - place
 SETUP_REPAIR_PHASES:
   description: >
     Passed as -phases to repair_timing. This should be a string of setup
-- 
2.53.0

